title radial_paint adds the circle beside the linear gradient family
prompt recur the autonomous loop: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Rye-first, green-witnessed, send each increment
think Read the road -- REMEMBER live edge, the 1024-round itinerary, the eight-season double-seat, the crypto-parity wave. Live edge is Season G open-media: image/gradient_paint.rye now paints a positioned gradient onto a real image along all four LINEAR directions (horizontal, vertical, and the diagonal pair). The prior lap's own recommend named a radial gradient as the next Lindy-first crux.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the linear gradient family is whole; the other major CSS gradient shape is RADIAL, where a pixel's ramp position is its distance FROM the box center rather than ALONG one axis. One coherent, bounded rung that opens the circle beside the line -- a surface renders both for years, so it is durable, and it is the hardest-still-tractable move (an integer square root, not a float) that completes the gradient family's two shapes.
think Compose not braid, unchanged: color_ramp_stops.sample_checked DECIDES each pixel's color, qoi owns the RGBA target, color composites src-over; this new module image/radial_paint.rye only ROUTES each pixel to its radial position and writes it -- no new color math, no new codec. A sibling file (its own canvas/pixel_at helpers) exactly as gradient_paint.rye and shape.rye each keep their own, rather than braiding a shared surface.
think The routing stays integer fixed-point so a disc is deterministic across targets. Doubled coordinates (2*cx - (w-1)) keep the center exact for odd dimensions and exactly between two pixels for even ones without a fraction. d2 = dx2*dx2 + dy2*dy2; the farthest corner sits max_d2 = (w-1)^2 + (h-1)^2 away (all four corners equidistant from the true center); p = isqrt(d2 * pos_max^2 / max_d2), so the center reads 0 and a corner reads isqrt(pos_max^2) = pos_max exactly.
think Overflow proven bounded: dx2,dy2 <= 8191 so each square <= ~6.7e7 and d2 <= ~1.34e8; d2 * pos_max^2 (65025) <= ~8.7e12 stays inside u64 (the multiply and the isqrt both u64). isqrt is bit-by-bit, seeded at 1<<62 and shrinking two bits per step, so at most 32 iterations -- bounded. Box bound-checked once up front in u64; ramp validated once before any pixel, so a refusal paints nothing (all-or-nothing, never a half-painted ring).
obs Refusals by name: BadStripDims (zero dimension), StripTooSmall (single-pixel box, no radial direction), RadialOutOfBounds, and every color_ramp_stops refusal -- each having painted nothing (proven by re-scanning the canvas all-white after a refusal).
obs Selftest proves it on metal, FIRST GREEN no reds: the center pixel is the first control and every corner the last byte-for-byte; the four edge midpoints share one constant ring color (a true circle, neither center nor corner); the position grows with the radius (the ring blends less toward the last control than a corner); uneven positions bend the disc where even spacing cannot (green at 200 vs 128 read differently on the same ring, MEASURED); the disc round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte; a sub-rectangle paints only its own box; a non-square 7x3 box still centers and corners exactly; determinism byte-for-byte.
obs Gates: no key, no signature, no funds, no provisioning -- fully agent-doable, no custody gate reached this lap.
obs Rota lap deep-read context/SILO_TECHNIQUE.md (item 22) -- the CSS radial-gradient concept enters siloed: the shape is ours, named plainly (radial_pos, paint_gradient_radial), and the thanks live in the witness header (gratitude/w3c-css-color.md), the thinking in one room and the thanksgiving in another.
loom witness=radial_paint_witness result=GREEN selftest_checks=center+corners+ring-symmetry+radius-monotonic+bend+roundtrip+nonsquare+refusals
file image/radial_paint.rye new module: paint_gradient_radial, radial_pos, isqrt_u64, and a selftest proving center/corners/rings/radius/bend/round-trip on metal
file tools/radial_paint_witness.rish new witness: builds the module, runs the selftest, greps the GREEN line, the ring-constant, radius-monotonic, bend, and round-trip proofs
file image/README.md names radial_paint.rye beside gradient_paint.rye (docs-sync)
file crux/REMEMBER.md moved live edge and Git nib forward to the radial rung
recommend keep-going the gradient family now paints both shapes (linear and radial); next Lindy-first crux could be the CONIC gradient (position by angle around a center, the third CSS gradient shape) or a radial-with-named-center helper (the center a caller names rather than the box center)
